1. Project Background and Business Need 
Healthcare organizations generate large amounts of operational and financial data through 
patient encounters, medical procedures, payer records, and organizational activities. When this 
information is not properly organized and analyzed, hospital managers may experience 
difficulties monitoring patient flow, understanding healthcare costs, identifying operational 
inefficiencies, and making informed decisions the Hospital Operations, Cost & Patient Flow 
Intelligence project aims to use the datasets provided for the internship assignment to support the 
analysis of hospital operations, patient encounters, procedures, and cost-related information. The 
project brings together different technical workstreams, including data analytics, data science, 
machine learning engineering, and generative AI, to develop a healthcare intelligence solution. 
The project management function will coordinate the activities of these workstreams, monitor 
progress, manage risks, and support the successful delivery of the project within the assigned 
timeframe. 
2. Project Objectives 
The project aims to: 
1. Coordinate the development of a healthcare intelligence solution using the datasets 
provided for the assignment. 
2. Support the analysis of patient encounters, procedures, payer information, and available 
cost-related data. 
3. Identify operational patterns and potential inefficiencies in patient flow through the 
analysis conducted by the technical teams. 
4. Ensure that data quality issues, assumptions, and limitations are documented by the 
relevant work stream members. 
5. Coordinate activities across the technical workstreams and monitor progress against 
agreed schedules and milestones. 
6. Establish project management procedures for risk management, quality assurance, 
communication, and change control. 
7. Ensure that project outputs are properly documented, reviewed, and prepared for final 
presentation and handover. 
3. Project Scope 
3.1 In Scope 
The project will cover the following activities: 
 Project initiation, planning, and coordination. 
 Stakeholder identification and communication. 
 Coordination of the initial review of the supplied healthcare datasets. 
 Documentation and monitoring of data quality findings. 
 Development and maintenance of the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). 
 Preparation of the project schedule and Gantt chart. 
 Resource planning and preparation of an estimated project budget. 
 Coordination and monitoring of the data analytics, data science, machine learning, and 
generative AI workstreams. 
 Risk, issue, and change management. 
 Quality assurance and testing coordination. 
 Monitoring project progress and managing dependencies. 
 Stakeholder review, final documentation, presentation, and project handover. 
3.2 Out of Scope 
The following activities are excluded from the project: 
 Deploying the solution in a live hospital environment. 
 Accessing or modifying actual hospital production systems. 
 Making clinical diagnoses or treatment recommendations. 
 Replacing existing hospital information management systems. 
 Publishing patient names, addresses, or other unnecessary personal identifiers. 
 Making unsupported claims about actual hospital performance or patient outcomes. 
