9. Project Governance and Communication 
The Project Management Intern will coordinate project planning, progress monitoring, 
documentation, and communication across all workstreams. 
Each workstream lead will be responsible for providing updates on assigned activities, reporting 
challenges, identifying risks, and communicating any changes that may affect project delivery. 
Project progress updates will capture: 
 Activities completed. 
 Activities currently in progress. 
 Upcoming activities and milestones. 
 Delayed activities and their causes. 
 Outstanding issues and identified risks. 
 Decisions required and corrective actions. 
 Responsible persons and agreed action dates. 
Any significant change to project scope, schedule, or resource requirements must be documented 
and submitted to the appropriate supervisor or programme contact for review before it is treated 
as approved. 
Project documentation will be maintained in an organized shared workspace to support 
accountability, collaboration, and final handover. 
All project members must observe data protection requirements. Patient-identifiable information 
must not be included in public repositories, screenshots, presentations, or other materials unless 
explicitly authorized and appropriately protected. 
